            <ArticleTitle>It Takes an Academic Village: The Library's Role in Supporting Interprofessional Communication through a Book Club.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-48</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02763869.2017.1259903</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Book clubs offer a unique opportunity to support interprofessional learning on academic campuses. The purpose of this article is to discuss how a health sciences library partnered with the Center for Interprofessional Healthcare Education to develop a book club that fosters interprofessional communication. The article includes a discussion of the opportunities, approach, results, and challenges.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
